# Interface Design Principles

These principles guide the development of our design system components and overall interface design.

## Core Principles

### 1. Task-Focused Design
- Components should help, never distract from the task
- Design for habitual use and muscle memory
- Understand gestures: Actions that become automatic through use

### 2. Modeless & Monotonous
- Components must be modeless - same gesture always yields same result
- One clear way to accomplish each action
- Avoid state-dependent behavior that could surprise users

### 3. Reliability
- Never lose user work or data
- Implement proper error handling and recovery
- Save state automatically where appropriate

### 4. Efficiency & Simplicity
- Optimize for minimal interaction time
- Remove unnecessary complexity
- Follow GOMS model principles for interaction design

### 5. Testing-Driven
- All components must be tested with real users
- Iterate based on user feedback
- Document known use cases and edge cases

### 6. Visual Appeal
- Clean, consistent design language
- Pleasant messaging and interactions
- Visual design supports function, never overshadows it

## Implementation Guidelines

### Component Structure
- Components should be in [src/components](mdc:src/components)
- Each component needs clear documentation
- Include usage examples and props documentation

### State Management
- Minimize component state
- Use controlled components where possible
- Document state changes and side effects

### Accessibility
- All components must be keyboard accessible
- Follow ARIA best practices
- Support screen readers

### Performance
- Optimize render performance
- Lazy load when appropriate
- Monitor bundle size impact

### Documentation
- Document all props and variants
- Include accessibility notes
- Provide usage guidelines and examples

## File Structure Reference
- [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) - Main application entry
- [src/components](mdc:src/components) - Component library
- [src/lib](mdc:src/lib) - Utilities and helpers
- [src/styles](mdc:src/styles) - Global styles and themes

These principles should be reflected in all code reviews and component implementations.
